(A) THE SCATTER IS NOT ONE NUMBER: it splits into a per-galaxy OFFSET and a within-galaxy SHAPE residual
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  N = 139 galaxies, 2678 points
  total vertical rms 0.1319 dex  =  WITHIN-galaxy 0.0715 dex  (+)  BETWEEN-galaxy 0.1109 dex, in quadrature
  median within-galaxy rms of a single galaxy: 0.0601 dex
  [PASS] 117B (a structural result, new here) most of the RAR's scatter is a per-galaxy NORMALISATION offset, not a failure of the relation's shape.  Splitting the residual into a between-galaxy and a within-galaxy part gives 0.111 dex and 0.072 dex: a galaxy sits off the relation as a whole nearly twice as far as its own points scatter about themselves.  That is exactly the signature of distance, inclination and mass-to-light errors, all of which move a galaxy bodily   (within 0.0715, between 0.1109, quadrature 0.1319 against the total 0.1327)

